{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","x":-2600,"y":-1380,"width":1600,"height":250,"text":"# Renovation Planner product discovery\n\n**Decision:** validate continuity plus explainable next-action guidance for Obsidian-using homeowners.\n\nOpen the full paper: [[renovation-planner-product-discovery]]"},
		{"id":"evidence-group","type":"group","x":-2600,"y":-1000,"width":1600,"height":2050,"label":"1 · Customer evidence","color":"4"},
		{"id":"vision","type":"file","x":-2500,"y":-880,"width":650,"height":300,"file":"docs/product/Product Vision.md"},
		{"id":"problem","type":"file","x":-1750,"y":-880,"width":650,"height":300,"file":"docs/product/Problem Definition.md"},
		{"id":"evidence-summary","type":"file","x":-2500,"y":-480,"width":650,"height":300,"file":"docs/product/research/renovation-planner-user-research-synthesis.md"},
		{"id":"market-study","type":"link","x":-1750,"y":-480,"width":650,"height":300,"url":"https://www.houzz.com/magazine/2026-u-s-houzz-and-home-study-renovation-trends-stsetivw-vs~185090855"},
		{"id":"firsthand","type":"link","x":-2500,"y":-80,"width":650,"height":300,"url":"https://www.create-enjoy.com/2018/03/3-ways-we-budget-for-reno-projects.html"},
		{"id":"reddit-evidence","type":"text","x":-1750,"y":-80,"width":650,"height":510,"text":"## Public discussion pattern\n\nThe archived synthesis records users cycling among Excel, Notion, task apps, phone folders, contractor PDFs, camera rolls, and memory.\n\n**Limitation:** Reddit returned HTTP 403 during the 2026-09-09 recheck. Treat those rows as prior secondary captures, not independently reverified quotations."},
		{"id":"support","type":"text","x":-2500,"y":360,"width":650,"height":560,"text":"## Supporting evidence\n\n- Fragmentation repeats across source types.\n- A firsthand spreadsheet became stale during execution.\n- 75% of surveyed Houzz renovators set a budget; 37% exceeded it.\n- Scope changes and upgraded materials contributed to overruns.\n- Low-friction capture and progressive detail matter."},
		{"id":"counter","type":"text","x":-1750,"y":530,"width":650,"height":390,"text":"## Counterevidence\n\n- New low-cost apps already combine rooms, budgets, receipts, tasks, and photos.\n- magicplan already links spatial capture, quantities, estimates, and scopes.\n- Spreadsheets remain sufficient for many small jobs.\n- No evidence yet proves willingness to pay."},
		{"id":"alternatives-group","type":"group","x":-800,"y":-1000,"width":1400,"height":2050,"label":"2 · Alternatives","color":"2"},
		{"id":"improvised","type":"text","x":-700,"y":-880,"width":1200,"height":300,"text":"## Main substitute\n\n**Spreadsheet + folders + messages + camera roll + memory**\n\nFamiliar, flexible, and often free. Its weakness is not any single tool; it is the maintenance of relationships among them."},
		{"id":"magicplan","type":"link","x":-700,"y":-480,"width":550,"height":300,"url":"https://magicplan.app/pricing"},
		{"id":"planner5d","type":"link","x":-50,"y":-480,"width":550,"height":300,"url":"https://planner5d.com/pricing"},
		{"id":"home-stories","type":"link","x":-700,"y":-80,"width":550,"height":300,"url":"https://home-stories.12f.dk/"},
		{"id":"renosaur","type":"link","x":-50,"y":-80,"width":550,"height":300,"url":"https://renosaur.app/"},
		{"id":"pro-tools","type":"text","x":-700,"y":320,"width":1200,"height":290,"text":"## Professional platforms\n\nBuildBook, JobTread, and Houzz Pro demonstrate deep connected workflows, but their CRM, accounting, client, and business operations make them excessive and expensive for the primary homeowner."},
		{"id":"white-space","type":"text","x":-700,"y":710,"width":1200,"height":210,"text":"## White space hypothesis\n\nHomeowner-first + renovation-specific + spatially connected + local/open + explainable guidance."},
		{"id":"opportunity-group","type":"group","x":800,"y":-1000,"width":1800,"height":880,"label":"3 · Chosen opportunity","color":"5"},
		{"id":"opportunity","type":"text","x":900,"y":-880,"width":1600,"height":290,"text":"# Continuity plus guidance\n\nPreserve the relationships among property areas, work, quantities, costs, materials, people, decisions, and documents—then use that context to identify the next useful decision or action."},
		{"id":"business","type":"text","x":900,"y":-490,"width":760,"height":250,"text":"## Immediate value\n\nA local project structure, spatially derived quantity/cost, and linked evidence help the first user before any advantage compounds."},
		{"id":"advantage","type":"text","x":1740,"y":-490,"width":760,"height":250,"text":"## Advantage hypothesis\n\nUser-owned property history plus homeowner-tested, explainable planning rules. This is a hypothesis, not an established moat."},
		{"id":"journey-group","type":"group","x":800,"y":80,"width":1800,"height":970,"label":"4 · First-value journey","color":"3"},
		{"id":"journey","type":"text","x":900,"y":200,"width":1600,"height":280,"text":"# Core journey\n\nCapture intention → valid incomplete project → optional plan → Room/Area → work/material requirement → derived quantity and cost → unresolved decision → next action → preserve what changed"},
		{"id":"scope","type":"text","x":900,"y":580,"width":760,"height":350,"text":"## Included in validation\n\n- One homeowner and one project\n- Optional image/PDF reference\n- Room or Area\n- One material requirement\n- Quantity/cost provenance\n- One explainable next action\n- User-owned source artifacts"},
		{"id":"excluded","type":"text","x":1740,"y":580,"width":760,"height":350,"text":"## Excluded\n\n- New prototype\n- 3D/rendering\n- Contractor CRM or accounting\n- Payments or marketplace\n- Real-time collaboration\n- Broad scheduling/procurement automation\n- AI construction advice"},
		{"id":"architecture-group","type":"group","x":2800,"y":-1000,"width":1700,"height":2050,"label":"5 · Architecture and data flow","color":"6"},
		{"id":"sdd","type":"file","x":2900,"y":-880,"width":1500,"height":300,"file":"docs/development/sdds/obsidian-renovation-planner-SDD.md"},
		{"id":"architecture","type":"text","x":2900,"y":-480,"width":1500,"height":480,"text":"## Existing flow\n\nObsidian views\n→ Presentation (Vue/Pinia/Konva)\n→ Application commands and queries\n→ Domain and core engines\n→ Repository ports\n→ Obsidian infrastructure\n→ Markdown notes + `.rpgeo` sidecars + plugin data\n\nThe vault remains the source of truth."},
		{"id":"model","type":"text","x":2900,"y":100,"width":720,"height":430,"text":"## Built foundation\n\nProject → Plan → Calibration → Zones → Assets/Requirements → Quantities → Costs\n\nStable IDs, explicit commands, versioned persistence, derived values, and readable source notes support trustworthy continuity."},
		{"id":"gap","type":"text","x":3680,"y":100,"width":720,"height":430,"text":"## Discovery gap\n\nThe technical MVP validates geometry → quantity → cost. It does not yet validate the full North Star: work, sequence, decisions, and next-action guidance remain incomplete or reserved.\n\nArchitecture is necessary evidence, not customer validation."},
		{"id":"delivery-group","type":"group","x":-800,"y":1250,"width":1400,"height":1050,"label":"6 · Honest handoff","color":"1"},
		{"id":"supported","type":"text","x":-700,"y":1370,"width":1200,"height":320,"text":"## Evidence supports\n\n- Fragmentation is recurrent.\n- Budget and scope drift matter.\n- Place, work, cost, and evidence need links.\n- Progressive detail is valuable.\n- Advanced visualization is not the core opportunity."},
		{"id":"unknown","type":"text","x":-700,"y":1790,"width":1200,"height":390,"text":"## Still unknown\n\n- Reachable Obsidian-renovator segment\n- Natural mental model\n- Maintenance during active work\n- Guidance comprehension and trust\n- Willingness to pay\n- Retention after project completion\n\n**No primary research or live-vault verification was performed.**"},
		{"id":"experiment-group","type":"group","x":800,"y":1250,"width":1800,"height":1050,"label":"7 · Next experiment","color":"1"},
		{"id":"experiment","type":"text","x":900,"y":1370,"width":1600,"height":410,"text":"# Eight artifact-led interviews\n\nAsk each participant to show a real spreadsheet, quote, plan, photo set, and decision trail. Reconstruct one room → work → quote → cost → evidence path. Then organize that case in the existing plugin and interpret one deterministic recommendation.\n\nNo new prototype."},
		{"id":"threshold","type":"text","x":900,"y":1880,"width":1600,"height":300,"text":"## Disproof thresholds · four weeks\n\n8 onboarded → 6 represent a live project → 4 maintain it for two weeks → 4 explain the recommendation and evidence → 3 commit at a stated one-time price.\n\nMaintenance or comprehension failure disproves the workflow; payment failure weakens the business model."}
	],
	"edges":[
